      "class": "DepictionStackView",
      "tabname": "Usage",
      "views": [
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Check it"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "```\nshiv-ortam --ajan-sina\n```\n\nFrom **shivtools**: checks client → server → attach → ObjC and prints the frida version it talks to."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Known issue on RootHide"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "frida 17 can bring **SpringBoard** down on about the third attach in a row; the device drops into safe mode and comes back in one go. Apps are fine, and frida 16 or rootless are not affected. frida 17 wants a memory-hooking API from the jailbreak that RootHide does not offer yet. Batch your SpringBoard work."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Clients"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "A frida client must match the **major** version: use frida-tools 17 on your computer. The client inside shivtools (`shivfrida`) is already built for 17."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Going back to 16"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "Remove this package, then install `re.frida.server` 16.1.4 from the RootHide repo."
        }
      ]
    },
